atlas external

architecture retained-shared-conversation
  canonical_name RetainedSharedConversation
  family external
  domain External / Retained Conversation
  layer external
  semantic_question What visible conversation text can be recovered from an already observed ChatGPT share without executing its scripts or treating historical text as current authority?
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tools/shared-conversation.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tests/shared-conversation.test.mjs
  consumes ForeignObservation
  publishes RetainedConversationText
  invariant The reader requires an allowed HTTP 200 observation and a matching body SHA-256 before decoding the retained JSON stream table.
  invariant The reader selects the shared route and checks its conversation identity against the source URL; user text and visible assistant text retain role, sequence and message identity.
  invariant Source scripts never execute; system and tool messages, tool calls, hidden messages and nonvisible channels are omitted with counts.
  internal_calculus A bounded JSON string scanner reads the first supported shared-route stream table. Indexed fields select the linear conversation without recursively expanding unrelated page state. Literal search and pagination operate only on extracted visible text.
  witness components/BonfyreProject/tests/shared-conversation.test.mjs checks role and channel separation, inert source scripts, exact message reads, pagination, identity mismatch, duplicate identity, digest drift and denied observations.
  known_gap The reader supports the observed inline indexed-table format only; deferred or changed streaming formats refuse and attachments and unshared branches are not recovered.
  known_gap The reusable BonfyreProject tool is available through Bun; a native command and MCP dispatch binding have not been added.
  forbidden_inference A recovered conversation -> current instructions, verified claims, attached file contents, current external availability or permission to send or publish.

interaction foreign-observation-to-shared-conversation
  source foreign-twin
  destination retained-shared-conversation
  relation decodes_retained_observation
  preserves Source URL, retained body digest, receipt path, observation time and individual message identity.
  drops Page executable code, unrelated application metadata, hidden channels and nontext attachment bodies.
  forbidden_inference A readable historical message -> a verified present capability or action authority.
